    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12371244/comment/12986844",
          "id": "12986844",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "I didn't find a way to check if an Ant directory is empty, and even if there is a way, the extract process can still fail in the middle. So maybe an alternative solution is to extract the files in ExtractReuters to a tmp directory first, and rename it if everything succeeds. Also, always delete the target dir at startup. That way, if extraction fails, the directory doesn't exist, and if it does exist, we know it's ok (unless manually tempered, but that's not for us to solve).\n\nWhat do you think?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "created": "2011-01-26T04:52:26.535+0000",
          "updated": "2011-01-26T04:52:26.535+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12371244/comment/12986867",
          "id": "12986867",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=doronc",
            "name": "doronc",
            "key": "doronc",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738"
            },
            "displayName": "Doron Cohen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Gaza"
          },
          "body": "Seems ok to me.\n\nbq. .. ExtractReuters to a tmp directory first, and rename it if everything succeeds. Also, always delete the *target* dir at startup\n\nshould be \"always delete the *tmp* dir at start\" ?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=doronc",
            "name": "doronc",
            "key": "doronc",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=doronc&avatarId=12738"
            },
            "displayName": "Doron Cohen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Gaza"
          },
          "created": "2011-01-26T07:04:05.883+0000",
          "updated": "2011-01-26T07:04:05.883+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12371244/comment/12986887",
          "id": "12986887",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "yes you're right :). If the target exists, the code should fail - we're not supposed to call it from Ant anyway, and so if it's indeed called, it may discover a bug in the build.xml, and if it's called by a standalone program, I think it'd be better to fail so as to indicate the caller that the dir exists - maybe he'll want to delete and re-create it.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "created": "2011-01-26T08:12:24.338+0000",
          "updated": "2011-01-26T08:12:24.338+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12371244/comment/12986909",
          "id": "12986909",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
            "key": "shaie",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Shai Erera",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Jerusalem"
          },
          "body": "Since ExtractReuters deletes all the files under the outputDir in its ctor, I didn't fail its main() if the directory exists. I've done some re-formatting to the class, but the relevant changes are under main().\n\nCommitted revision 1063640 (3x).\nCommitted revision 1063647 (trunk).\n\nThanks Doron and Grant !",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=shaie",
            "name": "shaie",
